        ("ROA decomposition?",
         "ROA = NPAT / total assets = profit margin (NPAT / (NII + NIR)) x asset utilisation ((NII + NIR) / total assets). Margin shows cost and tax control; utilisation shows gross yield on assets."),
        ("DuPont ROE for banks?",
         "ROE = NPAT / equity = profit margin x asset utilisation x leverage (total assets / equity). Equivalently ROE = ROA x equity multiplier."),
        ("Why is a bank's leverage not simply a strategy to boost ROE?",
         "Bank leverage is constrained by regulatory capital requirements, not freely chosen. It can jump when losses cut equity or deposits surge, so a higher equity multiplier can signal weakness rather than strategy."),
